kamerplanter#1302 — a pin assertion whose path filter excludes the very file
whose pin it asserts, so it cannot fire on the pull request that changes it.

Named in nolte/pre-commit-hooks#11 as one of the defects this hook was built
from, and required there as falsification: the hook must be RED on the pre-fix
state, not merely installed.

  red/    git show 421de1d2d^:.github/workflows/security-nuclei-templates.yml
          git show 421de1d2d^:.github/renovate-pins.yaml
  green/  git show 421de1d2d:.github/workflows/security-nuclei-templates.yml
          git show 421de1d2d^:.github/renovate-pins.yaml

  fix     421de1d2d  fix(ci): refuse a workflow that reads a path its own
                     filter excludes (#1316)

Both files are verbatim; nothing was added to them, because a provenance header
would shift the line numbers the assertion keys on. `.github/renovate-pins.yaml`
is carried because the fifth shape resolves read paths against the checkout's
TRACKED files: without it the reference is not a path and the defect does not
reproduce.

Expected: red/ reports `uncovered_path_reference` at line 74 of
security-nuclei-templates.yml; green/ reports nothing for that file.
